---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '25 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use · Belal Zaky"
  description="Terms of use for Mission Control, a personal single-user desktop dashboard that reads bank statement files exported by hand."
>
  <article class="legal container container--prose">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="legal-dek">
        These terms cover <strong>Mission Control</strong>, a personal desktop application I built
        and use myself. It is not a commercial product and it is not offered to anyone else.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What the application is</h2>
      <p>
        Mission Control is a desktop dashboard written and operated by Belal Zaky, an individual
        based in London, United Kingdom. It runs entirely on my own computer. One part of it reads
        bank statement files I export myself, so that I can see my own spending.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Me, and only me. There is no public version, no hosted version, no sign-up, no accounts, and
        no way for another person to use it. Nothing about it is sold, licensed, distributed or
        advertised. If any of that changes, these terms will be rewritten first.
      </p>

      <h2>What it does with financial data</h2>
      <p>
        The application has no connection to any bank and no ability to obtain data from one. It
        reads CSV statement files that I download from my own online banking and open in it myself.
        Nothing enters it any other way.
      </p>
      <p>
        It has no payment capability. It cannot move money, set up transfers, alter standing orders,
        or change anything at a bank.
      </p>
      <p>
        My relationship with my bank is governed by the bank's own terms. Nothing on this page
        overrides them. How the imported data is handled once it is on my computer is described in
        the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The application is provided as-is. It is a personal tool, written for my own use, with no
        guarantee of accuracy, availability, or fitness for any purpose. Figures it displays are for
        my own reference and are not financial advice, accounting records, or a substitute for
        statements issued by my bank. Where the application and the bank disagree, the bank is right.
      </p>

      <h2>No third-party access</h2>
      <p>
        Because there is no hosted service, there is nothing for anyone else to sign up to, log into,
        or misuse. If source code for the application is ever published, it will be published without
        credentials and without data.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may change if what the application does changes. The date at the top reflects the
        current version. An earlier version described reading bank data through a licensed account
        information provider; that route was never used and has been removed from the application.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Belal Zaky — <a href="mailto:hello@belalzaky.uk">hello@belalzaky.uk</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-title {
      font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    }
  }

  .legal-dek {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 55ch;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
